From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:45:41 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: usb: samsung,s2mm005: describe the source and
 host roles

The S2MM005 firmware also attaches as the source and as the host, with
VBUS from a supply outside the chip. Say what the connector then needs:
its vbus-supply, and a USB role switch on its high speed port.

Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/samsung,s2mm005.yaml | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/samsung,s2mm005.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/samsung,s2mm005.yaml
index 16e446fbd9..2318f2643f 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/samsung,s2mm005.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/samsung,s2mm005.yaml
@@ -13,8 +13,10 @@ description:
   The S2MM005 is a USB Type-C port controller with a USB Power Delivery
   policy engine running in its own firmware, controlled over I2C. As a sink
   it negotiates a power contract with the source by itself; the host reads
-  the attach state and the contract. It raises its open-drain interrupt line
-  while an event is pending.
+  the attach state and the contract. As a source it relies on the VBUS
+  supply of the connector, and as a dual role data port on a USB role
+  switch connected to the connector's high speed port. It raises its
+  open-drain interrupt line while an event is pending.
 
 properties:
   compatible:
